sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User
  participant WebApp as Web application
  participant CS as Content script
  participant BG as Background service worker
  participant Host as Native host GUI
  participant Engine as Processing engine
  participant HSM as HSM token
  participant API as Caller backend API

  WebApp->>CS: window.postMessage(HSM_SIGN_REQUEST)
  CS->>CS: Check origin allowlist
  CS->>CS: Validate schema and semantic rules
  CS->>BG: runtime.sendMessage(SIGNBRIDGE_SIGN_REQUEST)
  BG->>Host: connectNative(com.ase.signer)
  BG->>Host: postMessage(SignRequest)
  BG-->>CS: SignResponse(status=accepted)
  CS-->>WebApp: window.postMessage(HSM_SIGN_RESPONSE)

  Note over WebApp,API: The web app receives only an acknowledgment. Final results arrive through backend callbacks.

  Host->>User: Show request, token selector, PIN field
  User->>Host: Select token and approve signing
  Host->>Engine: process_request(request, session, key, cert)
  Engine->>Engine: resolve objects / groups
  Engine->>API: GET downloadUrl or use inline content
  API-->>Engine: Raw bytes
  Engine->>API: POST progress callback (optional)
  Engine->>HSM: PKCS#11 sign operation
  HSM-->>Engine: Signature or signed document
  Engine->>API: POST uploadUrl with raw signed bytes
  API-->>Engine: Upload HTTP result
  Engine->>API: POST onSuccess callback
  Host->>Host: Log completion and close window